  "post": {
    "caption": "One Cartier necklace is two crocodiles. The Mexican film star Maria Felix was a devoted Cartier client, and in 1975 Cartier made her a crocodile necklace. Legend says she brought a live baby crocodile to the boutique as a model. The two jointed crocodiles wrap around the neck, one covered in yellow diamonds and the other in emeralds, with over 2,000 stones in all. Each crocodile unclips and can be worn as a brooch. After she sold her jewels, Cartier bought the necklace back. The yellow crocodile alone holds 1,023 diamonds.",
